    {
      "id": "claim_bfe2c89490a44863baa56aa8a7c7f5dd",
      "statement": "Decision D-016 governs the proof chain: a downstream smoke test reuses prior PASS evidence when genuinely required and creates only the smallest temporary live integration to prove its own contract; temporary wiring is removed; a smoke dependency does not become production architecture; a downstream PASS must identify the upstream proof it relied on. The roadmap explicitly does not force every test to call every earlier component.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/00-control/DECISIONS.md#L54-L55",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f1a887417dec28f2a53c1b09c643fb9a5368b133890ed343547db9cd098706d3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/00-control/HX-ECO-SYSTEM-SMOKE-TEST-ROADMAP.md#L35-L49",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a7b430fd0b78f7a8991faac7fd39f5badc5227d34e3f53521e9fbb086947847b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1b32ed865da14119a75e728762f1625b",
      "statement": "The smoke roadmap defines five dependency types: foundation prerequisite (ecosystem state already established), prior smoke PASS (earlier component proof must be accepted), limited validation integration (temporary live connection required and removed afterward), companion gate (parent core PASS then UI/MCP PASS), and no component dependency (test stays standalone for fault isolation).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/00-control/HX-ECO-SYSTEM-SMOKE-TEST-ROADMAP.md#L51-L60",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aed07c79c8f8a948ff0e8f8ba9b9ffd1027fc464d95828a0020abf00a12543c4:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8e29c96013f34365bb7ee08d09430db5",
      "statement": "HX has two current evidence shapes: inline record evidence for HX-1/HX-2/HX-3 (proof recorded inside docs/02-server-records/ as exact commands/responses, accepted as prior_pass_evidence) and run-bundle evidence for HX-4 onward (created by hx-smoke-new, promoted by hx-smoke-promote, retained under docs/05-evidence/<sut>/<component>/<run-id>/ with manifest.md, result.txt, cleanup.txt, and supporting captures).",
