      "statement": "Reboot persistence is a separate gate performed after the functional test passes and cleanup completes: reboot the SUT, confirm the service returns active/enabled and required storage/configuration persists, then execute the minimum post-reboot functional proof defined for that component rather than automatically rerunning a large destructive or expensive test.",
