      "id": "claim_5c23fd00f27141b7b2884321486339db",
      "statement": "A downstream test may rely only on current proof. Material changes after a PASS (model alias/revision/dimension, embedding/reranker changes, Qdrant/database/vector-store upgrade or configuration, major API/MCP contract, routing behavior, SUT rebuild) can stale prior evidence and require revalidation before downstream reliance. Re-running a prerequisite creates a new evidence reference that downstream tests must cite.",
