    {
      "id": "claim_37aa4b9348534bfa9fed7f2c7602c9b3",
      "statement": "The smoke-testing system is a validation layer that does not create a container platform, second deployment plane, permanent cross-service integration mesh, general reverse-proxy requirement, new firewall/TLS/DNS/network architecture, production test data, automatic evidence commits, or a replacement for ecosystem architecture; a smoke dependency never becomes production architecture by default and operators must never infer permanent architecture from temporary smoke-test wiring.",
